It's been a whileが「久しぶり」
"It's been a while" means "long time no see".

132
00:15:29,824 --> 00:15:33,224
なんか、意外といけたわ。
Like, I actually managed to do it.

133
00:15:34,924 --> 00:15:37,624
1人で喋るのが難しいのじゃあ。
It's hard to talk all by myself, noja.

134
00:15:38,824 --> 00:15:40,424
難しかったなあ。
It was difficult...

135
00:15:41,824 --> 00:15:43,024
なんか...
Like...

136
00:15:45,324 --> 00:15:50,424
意外と...って感じだった。思ってたより喋れたかも。
I felt like, "Hey, unexpectedly..." Maybe I spoke better than I thought.

137
00:15:52,024 --> 00:15:59,824
Collabs with EN will help you English definitely. Yeah, yes, I think so, too.

138
00:16:00,624 --> 00:16:05,224
ねー、コラボするとー、のじゃイングリッシュの何倍もの経験値...
Yeah, doing collabs gives me many times more experience points than Noja English...

139
00:16:05,924 --> 00:16:07,524
1人で喋れてるの？本当？
Am I able to speak on my own? Really?

140
00:16:08,524 --> 00:16:13,624
なんか、わしてきにはやっぱ1人で喋るとどうしても出てこない単語とかがあるんじゃけれど...
For me, when I talk alone, there are always words I can't come up with, but...

141
00:16:14,224 --> 00:16:20,124
なんか、うーん、人とだとー、分かんない単語とかも補足的に喋ってくれるから乗っかるだけでいい。
Um, when I'm with someone, they help supply words I don't know, so I just need to ride along with it.

142
00:16:22,524 --> 00:16:27,424
PEAK配信途中まで見たけどメラチゲームセンス高いと思う。めっちゃ練習した！
"I watched the PEAK stream partway, I think Melachi has high game sense." I practiced so much!

143
00:16:27,524 --> 00:16:34,024
実ハ、実ハ昨日今日にPEAK配信やるよって言われた時点で1人でこそこそ練習してたのじゃ。
Actually, the moment I was told yesterday that we were doing a PEAK stream today, I was secretly practicing by myself, noja.

144
00:16:34,124 --> 00:16:45,024
I practice a lot. Yes, I practice PEAK game a lot before collab stream.

145
00:16:47,524 --> 00:16:49,024
配信初見。サンキューのじゃ！
"First time in stream." Thank you noja!

146
00:16:50,024 --> 00:16:56,224
なんかね、本当にゲーム苦手で、本当にゲーム苦手で、ゲームに一杯一杯になったら英語喋れんだろうなと思ったから...
Like, I'm really bad at games, so I thought if I get completely overwhelmed by the game, I wouldn't be able to speak English, so...

147
00:16:58,324 --> 00:17:04,224
そう、コミュニケーション取れんだろうなって思ってたから、PEAKはあまり切れなかった。切れなかったよ。
Yeah, I thought I wouldn't be able to communicate, so I couldn't really stay sharp in PEAK. I couldn't stay sharp.

148
00:17:04,324 --> 00:17:08,924
PEAKはそんな切れるような要素なかったな。なんか、「あー、わし下手ー」って思うこと多かったけど。
Though there wasn't really much reason to get mad in PEAK. I mostly just felt like, "Ah, I'm so bad at this."

149
00:17:09,524 --> 00:17:12,724
バク転ジャンプは、あの昨日練習した。うん。
The backflip jump, I practiced that yesterday. Yep.

150
00:17:14,024 --> 00:17:22,024
I practice jump, backflip jump yesterday. たまにできるぐらいになったのじゃ。
I practice jump, backflip jump yesterday. I got to the point where I can pull it off occasionally, noja.

151
00:17:25,524 --> 00:17:33,524
なんか、結構下手くそすぎるとさ、視聴者さんをイライラさせてしまうのが怖くてさ。
Like, I'm scared of frustrating the viewers if I'm way too bad at gaming.

152
00:17:34,524 --> 00:17:39,524
なんか、「うわ、こいつゲーム下手で見でイライラするなー」って思われたら嫌じゃから...
Because I'd hate for people to think, "Ugh, this person is so bad at games, it's frustrating to watch."

153
00:17:40,024 --> 00:17:45,524
だから、なんか、やったことないゲームは1時間ぐらいは練習するようにしてるんじゃけれど...
So I try to practice games I've never played for about an hour beforehand, but...

154
00:17:46,524 --> 00:17:48,824
あ、難しそうなゲームはね。
Ah, the difficult-looking ones, that is.

155
00:17:49,824 --> 00:17:50,624
そう。
Yeah.

156
00:17:51,524 --> 00:18:05,024
やっぱコミュニケーションに集中したかったから、I want communicate with senpai in English, so I practice PEAK a lot.
I really wanted to focus on communication after all, so "I want communicate with senpai in English, so I practice PEAK a lot."

157
00:18:06,024 --> 00:18:13,224
PEAKに一杯一杯になったらね、あの、普段喋らない言語で喋るみたいなのができなくなっちゃう。
If I get overwhelmed by PEAK, then I wouldn't be able to speak in a language I don't normally speak.

158
00:18:13,324 --> 00:18:20,824
ARKも練習した。ARKも練習した。あの、何やっけ、操作動画、初心者操作動画みたいなのを見て練習したんじゃけれど...
I practiced ARK too. I practiced ARK too. I watched, what was it, controls videos, like beginner controls tutorial videos to practice, but...

159
00:18:21,524 --> 00:18:33,524
本当になんか、あの、石を拾って、木をなんかから殴って、こう言うなんか斧を作ろうみたいなのじゃだけで、あのプテラテイムのところまでは見てないのじゃ。
It was really just stuff like picking up stones, punching trees, and making an axe. I didn't watch as far as taming a Pteranodon, noja.

160
00:18:34,024 --> 00:18:38,924
本当にもう初心者はまずこれをやれ、ドードーテイムだけ見のじゃ。
Really, I only watched the "Beginners do this first: Dodo taming" part, noja.

161
00:18:39,024 --> 00:18:45,524
んじゃから、それより先のとこまで行くと思わなくて、それより先のところすごい難しかったのじゃ。
So I didn't expect to go beyond that, and everything past that was super difficult, noja.

162
00:18:52,524 --> 00:19:01,024
そう、慣れたゲームじゃないとね、コラボに集中できないからね、予習はしてるんだけどね、やっぱ予習って1時間ぽっちじゃ正直足りないのじゃ。
Yeah, unless I'm used to the game, I can't focus on the collab, so I do prepare in advance, but honestly, just one hour of preparation isn't enough, noja.

163
00:19:02,524 --> 00:19:05,224
1時間ぽっちじゃ足りないのじゃ。
Just one hour isn't enough, noja.

164
00:19:06,024 --> 00:19:10,024
一応1人のサーバーで練習はしたんじゃけれどね。
I did practice on a solo server, though.

165
00:19:13,024 --> 00:19:13,924
Yes.

166
00:19:17,024 --> 00:19:22,524
のじゃ。初テイムも死んじゃったけどね。Yes, I'm beginner. そう、ドードーだけ練習した。
Noja. Though my first tamed dino died. "Yes, I'm beginner." Yeah, I only practiced Dodo.

167
00:19:25,524 --> 00:19:31,024
OK,じゃあ Let's start English study.
OK, then "Let's start English study."

168
00:19:31,224 --> 00:19:42,524
Maybe set a goal game to play with an EN senpai, like Keep Talking and Nobody Explodes. Speaking while under pressure can be a good test.

169
00:19:43,524 --> 00:19:50,924
まあ、そう。今後も、今後も頑張るのじゃ。今後も頑張るのじゃ。
Well, yeah. I'll do my best in the future too, noja. I'll keep trying my best, noja.

170
00:19:51,024 --> 00:20:00,024
早くお顔も見たい、そうだよね！You guys want to see my cute, cute, cute, cute, cute, really cute face, noja? I know.
"Can't wait to see your face too", right! "You guys want to see my cute, cute, cute, cute, cute, really cute face, noja? I know."

171
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:01,332
Oh, I know, I know.

172
00:20:01,432 --> 00:20:03,432
Yes, I know.

173
00:20:03,932 --> 00:20:08,532
You guys want to see my cute face, noja?

174
00:20:09,932 --> 00:20:15,832
Okay, then please like my channel! Please like my video!

175
00:20:17,632 --> 00:20:20,132
And...

176
00:20:20,632 --> 00:20:21,832
Wait.

177
00:20:21,932 --> 00:20:23,932
そして、待っ…待ちちなさい。
And wait... wait a moment.

178
00:20:24,032 --> 00:20:26,532
Thank you for membership gift!
Thank you for the membership gift!

179
00:20:27,732 --> 00:20:30,932
それでは高評価を押して待っていてくださいのじゃ！
So please hit the like button and wait, noja!

180
00:20:31,032 --> 00:20:37,032
Let's start English study stream, noja!
Let's start the English study stream, noja!

181
00:20:40,632 --> 00:20:44,232
やばい、面言のままだ、テキストが。
Oh no, the text is still set to that!

182
00:20:45,332 --> 00:20:52,532
Wait a minute. 英語の…うー…英語の…勉強…
Wait a minute. English... um... English... studying...

183
00:20:52,732 --> 00:20:54,832
あ、顔混ざってない。
Ah, my face mask didn't change!

184
00:20:55,732 --> 00:20:57,632
あー！のじゃ！
Ah! Noja!

185
00:20:59,332 --> 00:21:03,532
のじゃーー！外せなかった！
Nojaaa! I couldn't take it off!

186
00:21:04,532 --> 00:21:06,532
できなかったー！
I couldn't do it!

187
00:21:08,532 --> 00:21:10,532
取ろうと思ったの。
I was trying to take it off.

188
00:21:10,632 --> 00:21:21,032
I... I thought I already off my mask, but I didn't.
I... I thought I already took off my mask, but I didn't.

189
00:21:21,532 --> 00:21:23,732
できてなかったのじゃ。
I failed to do it, noja.

190
00:21:24,032 --> 00:21:28,032
Failed! 失敗…失敗したのじゃ。
Failed! A failure... It was a failure, noja.

191
00:21:32,432 --> 00:21:44,232
My favorite stream of the week always make me smile and brightness... brightens my week. Thank you, Noja!
My favorite stream of the week always makes me smile and brightens my week. Thank you, Noja!

192
00:21:44,232 --> 00:21:45,332
You're welcome, Noja!

193
00:21:46,532 --> 00:21:50,832
のじゃEnglish好きな人いてくれて嬉しい。初スパチャありがとなのじゃー！
I'm so glad there are people who like Noja English! Thank you for your first Superchat, noja!

194
00:21:51,532 --> 00:21:54,032
テレワークで見に来てくれてるのか。
Oh, you're watching while working remotely?

195
00:21:54,232 --> 00:21:58,232
早くない？お仕事開始。まだ7時20分じゃよ！
Isn't that early for starting work? It's only 7:20!

196
